<h2>How should the settings groups be laid out?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Same 12 fields, grouped as Profile / Preferences / Notifications / Security. One Save button submits everything in every option.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Stacked sections (recommended)</h3>
      <p>One scrolling page with a titled section per group, separated by dividers. Least change, no JS, everything still visible at once.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div class="label">Profile</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Preferences</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Time zone">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Language">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Theme">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Notifications</div>
          <p>[ ] Email &nbsp; [ ] Push &nbsp; [ ] Weekly digest</p>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Security</div>
          <p>[ ] Two-factor auth</p>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Session timeout (min)">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="API token">
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Card per group</h3>
      <p>Each group in its own bordered card with a heading. Stronger visual separation; still one page and one Save.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div class="placeholder"><strong>Profile</strong><br>Display name · Email · Avatar URL</div>
          <div class="placeholder"><strong>Preferences</strong><br>Time zone · Language · Theme</div>
          <div class="placeholder"><strong>Notifications</strong><br>Email · Push · Weekly digest</div>
          <div class="placeholder"><strong>Security</strong><br>2FA · Session timeout · API token</div>
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Sidebar / tabs</h3>
      <p>Group list on the left, one group visible at a time. Shortest screen, but needs JS to switch panels and hides fields from view.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Settings</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="display:flex">
          <div class="mock-sidebar"><strong>Profile</strong><br>Preferences<br>Notifications<br>Security</div>
          <div class="mock-content">
            <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name">
            <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email">
            <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
            <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
